EXTENSION "ARMDef_Through_the_Aegis_NorthernSeas_ThriceDeadNed" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, Through the Aegis - Thrice-Dead Ned"
    VERSION "0.5.1"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-06"
    DEPENDS_ON "ARMDef_Through_the_Aegis_Core_Ext"

    # Thrice-Dead Ned (Chapter Two: The Northern Seas, p22): one character, its stat lines verbatim fields.

    #ta81208af35fe439a384726 ^"Thrice-Dead Ned" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Role" STRING "Specialist"
            ^"Covenant" LIST [#t2b859a5f0c51942368a661 ^"The Northern Seas"]
            ^"Characteristics" STRING "Int –1 (1), Per –1, Pre –1, Com –1, Str +1, Sta +4 (2), Dex +1 (1), Qik 0"
            ^"Size" STRING "0"
            ^"Age" STRING "45 (45)"
            ^"Decrepitude" STRING "1 (2)"
            ^"Warping Score" STRING "0 (0)"
            ^"Virtues and Flaws" STRING "Covenfolk; Great Stamina, Rapid Convalescence, Warrior; No Sense of Direction, Weak Characteristics, Weakness (talking back to magi)"
            ^"Personality Trait" STRING "Loyal +3, Cheeky +2, Brave +1"
            ^"Combat" STRING "Dodge: Init –4, Attack n/a, Defense +3, Damage n/a Fist: Init –4, Attack +4, Defense +3, Damage +1 Kick: Init –5, Attack +5, Defense +3, Damage +4 Axe & Round Shield: Init –2, Attack +13, Defense +10, Damage +7 Crossbow: Init +3, Attack +12, Defense +6, Damage +8"
            ^"Soak" STRING "+11"
            ^"Fatigue Levels" STRING "OK, 0, –1, –3, –5, Unconscious"
            ^"Wound Penalties" STRING "–1 (1–5), –3 (6–10), –5 (11–15), Incapacitated (16–20), Dead (21+)"
            ^"Abilities" STRING "Area Lore: Normandy Coast 4 (monsters), Area Lore: Stonehenge’s Southern Coast 2 (monsters), Awareness 5 (in combat), Brawl 3 (Kick), Carouse 3 (with fighting friends), Chirurgy 5 (binding wounds), Crossbow 5 (crossbow), Organization Lore: Covenant of the Northern Seas 1 (personalities), English 5 (military talk), Folk Ken 1 (magi), Guile 2 (getting extra rations), Leadership 3 (in combat), French 3 (Norman), Order of Hermes Lore 3 (grogs), Single Weapon 7 (round shield), Stealth 3 (when armored), Survival 1 (when in a group), Swim 1 (staying afloat), Thrown Weapon 4 (knife)"
            ^"Equipment" STRING "Round Shield; Ax; Crossbow; Full Metal Scale Armor; Pack"
            ^"Encumbrance" STRING "4 (5)"
            ^"Appearance" STRING "Despite his years, his well-trained arms and shoulders still fill his armor well. His beard may be gray, his eyes a little rheumy, and he may be a little hard of hearing, but he has a lightness to his step and ready smile."
            ^"Source" STRING "Through the Aegis"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 22
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Thrice-Dead Ned is so called because he has very nearly died in the service of magi at least three times. He considers himself lucky, though others aren’t as sure. He has an astounding constitution that sees him recover from wounds that would have surely killed other men. Years of patching his own wounds have taught him the art of chirurgery and he sees that his fighting friends are well looked after.\n\nThrice-Dead Ned benefits from a Stamina of 4 +3 for Rapid Convalescence in all Wound Recovery Rolls, as detailed in ArM5, page 179. He does however have some Aging Points against a few of his characteristics, which puts him at risk during each winter.\n\nNed isn’t clever, but he isn’t stupid either. He knows he’s getting on a bit and prefers to use his crossbow from range, reloading while others keep danger at bay. Ned uses the Crossbow Ability from Lords of Men, page 138, and spans his crossbow using a belt hook."
    }

}
